.\" zvoltimeline(1) — manual page, mdoc. Kept true to the program by
.\" tests/man-check.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt ZVOLTIMELINE 1
.Os zvolrescue 0.9.15
.Sh NAME
.Nm zvoltimeline
.Nd the history of a ZFS pool from the transaction groups it still carries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads every transaction group (TXG) that still verifies on the members
of a pool, oldest to newest, and turns the differences between them
into a history: when each dataset, volume and snapshot was created,
renamed, destroyed or cloned, and what its properties were.
A clone promoted over its origin is a
.Ql promoted
event; the snapshots the promotion moved to it are renamed, and say
so.
Read only from after a promotion, the dataset promoted is a clone
promoted since, and the one it was promoted over was created, not
cloned: snapshots older than the dataset that holds them came with a
promotion.
It reads the members the way
.Xr zvolrescue 1
does, never writes to them, and can write an evidence log the same
way.
.Pp
A TXG whose MOS cannot be walked is an
.Ql unreadable
event that says why.
A TXG written before a lower one already read belongs to a line of
history an import with rewind left behind; it is an
.Ql abandoned
event and is not read into the history.
The hosts the labels name are
.Ql host
events, each at the newest label that names it.
One read in part \(em part of its dataset tree did not read \(em is
counted as read in part, and what lies there is taken as it was at the
TXG before; it is not destroyed there, and a dataset destroyed later is
last seen at the last TXG it was read at.
What such a TXG, or the oldest one read, could not see is not created
at the next one: it is dated by when it was made, and said to have been
there unread.
A property that could not be read at one TXG is not a change, and
.Fl -pending
on a TXG read in part is a floor.
.Pp
The pool members are given as devices, or as image files with
.Fl -image .
The
.Sx POOL MEMBER OPTIONS
and the global options are those of
.Xr zvolrescue 1
and are listed here in brief.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -from Ar txg
Oldest transaction group to read; default the oldest that verifies.
.It Fl -to Ar txg
Newest transaction group to read; default the newest that verifies.
.It Fl -dataset Ar name | guid
Only events about this object: a dataset or snapshot name it had at
any TXG, or its GUID, in hex as this tool prints it or in decimal as
.Ql zfs get guid
does.
It is followed through its renames by GUID.
What is about the pool rather than one object stays: what
.Fl -pending
reports, and a TXG whose MOS could not be walked.
A name or GUID that is in none of the transaction groups read is said,
and the exit status is 3.
.It Fl -pending
Also report how much space is held by things ZFS has finished with
but has not freed.
While a block is still accounted for there, it has not been
reallocated.
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar file
Write the report to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
A pipe or a terminal is written to and not read back: the evidence
log records a file it wrote, with its hash, and the report itself.
Refused, with exit 5, if it is anything the run reads or shares bytes
with it: a member under any name, a map, the hints, a device a member
is on, or the path a log goes to.
.It Fl f , Fl -format Ar text | json
Output format; text is the default.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Also report changes of a property \(em
.Ql volsize ,
.Ql volblocksize ,
the encryption suite \(em as
.Ql property
events; without it they are counted and not shown.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Leave out the count of property changes not shown.
.It Fl -evidence-log Ar file
Append a JSON Lines evidence log to
.Ar file .
.It Fl -hash-inputs
Also record the SHA-256 of every input in the evidence log; a device is
not read again for it (SPEC N-10), and its size is recorded instead.
.It Fl -no-color
Disable colour in text output.
.It Fl -debug , Fl -debug-log Ar file
Trace every read decision, to standard error or to
.Ar file .
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh POOL MEMBER OPTIONS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
.Fl -image Ar file
(an image file that is a member; repeatable),
.Fl -hints Ar file
(the layout by hand),
.Fl -search-order
(try every member order the layout leaves open),
.Fl -pool-guid Ar guid
(which pool when several are found),
.Fl -assume-member Ar path Ns Op = Ns Ar guid
(a member whose labels are gone),
.Fl -ignore-unknown-features ,
.Fl -map Ar member Ns = Ns Ar mapfile
(the ddrescue mapfile an image was made with),
.Fl -device-may-fail
and
.Fl -surface-scan-on-device .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
0 success, 1 usage, 2 evidence unreadable, 3 nothing readable, or
nothing about the
.Fl -dataset
asked for, 5 refused, 7 the medium refused a read.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Everything the ring of two mirror members still tells, as JSON:
.Dl zvoltimeline -f json /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3
.Pp
What happened to one volume, with what its freed space still holds:
.Dl zvoltimeline --dataset pool/vm/disk0 --pending /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zvolreport 1 ,
.Xr zvolrescue 1
